(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[8 1 "// Descriptors (PY5c; CPython's Objects/descrobject.c, funcobject.c's classmethod and staticmethod,"] [9 1 "// classobject.c's method, typeobject.c's super and slot wrappers): bound methods, functions as"] [10 1 "// descriptors, classmethod, staticmethod, property, __slots__' members, super, the slot wrappers"] [11 1 "// that show a built-in type's slots as methods, and the attributes of types, functions and methods."] [24 1 "// Method is a bound method: a function and the object it is bound to."] [31 1 "// ClassMethod and StaticMethod wrap a callable."] [33 12 "// made by classmethod(...), not a built-in type's"] [47 1 "// Property is property(fget, fset, fdel, doc)."] [51 27 "// a subclass of property"] [61 1 "// Member is a __slots__ entry's descriptor."] [70 1 "// Super is super(type, obj)."] [79 1 "// slotWrapper is a built-in type's slot as a method (wrapper_descriptor)."] [88 1 "// mappingProxy is a type's __dict__ read only."] [91 11 "// the type whose __dict__ it is, or nil"] [92 11 "// the mapping, when it is no dict (mappingproxy(UserDict()))"] [95 1 "// proxied is the mapping behind p."] [119 1 "// newWrappers are the built-in types' __new__ objects, one each."] [127 1 "// slotWrappers keep one wrapper per type and name, so that int.__repr__ is int.__repr__ (enum compares"] [128 1 "// a class's methods with its data type's and object's; PY5e, part 2b)."] [131 1 "// slotWrapperFor is built-in type m's slot for the special method name, or nil."] [156 5 "// object's own slots take the instance itself, not a built-in subclass's value: object.__str__ of an"] [157 5 "// int subclass is repr(self), its class's __repr__ (queue 287: test_enum's __str__ = object.__str__)"] [163 2 "// the number protocol's binary methods (__add__, __radd__, __iadd__ ...): the Binary, RBinary and InPlace"] [164 2 "// slots, NotImplemented when they do not apply (PY6h's REQUEST, queue 200: test_asyncio reads int.__add__)"] [189 6 "// wrap_ternaryfunc_r: the operands swapped, the modulus third"] [202 22 "// wrap_indexargfunc"] [213 4 "// object_str: tp_repr, never the type's own __str__ (REQUEST of PY6g for PY6-core: a class with"] [214 4 "// __str__ = object.__str__, doctest's DocTestCase, recursed without end)"] [335 5 "// dict_subscript sees self's type: a subclass's d.__getitem__(k) calls its __missing__ as d[k] does"] [336 5 "// (queue 202: urllib.parse's _Quoter(safe).__getitem__ raised KeyError: test_http_cookies,"] [337 5 "// test_wsgiref's request_uri)"] [445 3 "// one object per type, so that object.__new__ is object.__new__ (enum's _find_new_ compares them;"] [446 3 "// PY5e, part 2b)"] [498 6 "// unicode__format__, long__format__, float___format__, complex___format__: an empty spec is the"] [499 6 "// subclass's str() (queue 287: int's gave the int's text, test_enum's overridden __str__)"] [504 19 "// object.__format__ is str(self), the instance's own __str__ (queue 287)"] [538 1 "// hackCheck is hackcheck: m's __setattr__ called on self, whose built-in base nearest to its type overrides it"] [539 1 "// (object.__setattr__(str, ...) would jump over type's own)."] [549 22 "// of the built-in bases one can reach here, only type overrides tp_setattro"] [556 1 "// objectDir is object.__dir__: the instance's dictionary's keys and its class's attributes."] [603 3 "// object's wrappers are made on demand (slotWrapperFor), add_operators' names here"] [626 1 "// superArgs are super()'s zero arguments: the running function's first argument and its __class__ cell."] [664 2 "// supercheck: a proxy's __class__ (a class it pretends to be an instance of)"] [691 2 "// method_reduce (classobject.c): getattr(self, the function's name)"] [706 2 "// functions as descriptors, bound methods"] [713 2 "// types.MethodType(func, instance) (method_new)"] [739 2 "// method_descr_get: a bound method is not bound again (gh-113157)"] [778 2 "// slot wrappers"] [815 2 "// classmethod, staticmethod (funcobject.c): a subclass's instance is an Instance around the Go value, so every"] [816 2 "// slot unwraps; __init__ copies the wrapped callable's attributes (functools_wraps) into the dict"] [842 19 "// a classmethod made by a program, not a built-in type's descriptor"] [868 3 "// a built-in type's classmethod_descriptor: a builtin_function_or_method bound to the class (dict.fromkeys)"] [926 3 "// descriptor_get_wrapped_attribute and its setter: the dict first, the callable's value kept there"] [971 2 "// property"] [1103 2 "// __slots__' members"] [1184 2 "// super"] [1231 5 "// a built-in type's method, or a method descriptor in a heap type's dict (methodDescrs: _ast's AST,"] [1232 5 "// queue 202c: super().__init__ in a node class's subclass)"] [1260 53 "// a subclass of super: its type called"] [1282 2 "// mappingproxy"] [1284 2 "// mappingproxy(mapping), over a dict (PY6a: enum's __members__); other mappings are the data model's"] [1292 3 "// an exact dict by its storage; a dict subclass (OrderedDict) as the mapping it is, so its repr and its"] [1293 3 "// comparison are its own (mappingproxy_new keeps the object; queue 278: inspect's Signature.parameters)"] [1297 3 "// mappingproxy_check_mapping: PyMapping_Check, not a list or a tuple"] [1310 2 "// a built-in type's own slots' wrappers (ownSlots, registry.go) are in its __dict__ too (PY5e, part 2b)"] [1318 14 "// a built-in type's attribute descriptors (type.__dict__['__annotations__']: annotationlib)"] [1350 2 "// mappingproxy_richcompare: the mapping's own comparison (queue 202: mappingproxy({}) == {} was False; test_re's"] [1351 2 "// test_getattr compares a pattern's groupindex with a dict)"] [1376 2 "// mappingproxy_or: the mappings beneath, a proxy's unwrapped on either side"] [1452 33 "// one object, as a static type's: pickle's memo shares it"] [1461 3 "// type_set_module: the class's __firstlineno__ goes with its old module (queue 278: inspect.getsource of"] [1462 3 "// _py_abc's ABCMeta, renamed into abc, raises OSError)"] [1504 21 "// inside the first mro()"] [1554 2 "// type_get_text_signature: the signature in tp_doc, for the types that have one here (func_new's clinic doc)"] [1558 19 "// a C type's tp_doc signature (arbace/pyctypes, queue 270b)"] [1570 33 "// type_mro: mro_implementation afresh, a metaclass's mro() builds on it"] [1604 3 "// recursive_issubclass's check_class"] [1629 1 "// checkSetSpecial is check_set_special_type_attr."] [1785 2 "// method_descriptor's members and getsets (descrobject.c's descr_members, method_getset; queue 286)"] [1819 2 "// __module__ is func.go's (PY6d's R5: the function's module), which this init's order let override this one"] [1822 1 "// excSlots are the __slots__ values of exceptions (an exception class's instances are *Exception, not"] [1823 1 "// *Instance): PY6a, by the integration's owner, for test_exceptions' slotted exception classes."] [1826 1 "// setTypeBases is type.__bases__'s setter (typeobject.c's type_set_bases; PY6b's request: typing.NamedTuple"] [1827 1 "// assigns a class's bases): a heap type's bases replaced by types of the same instance layout, its MRO and its"] [1828 1 "// subclasses' computed again and their slots refilled."] [1847 3 "// a reentrant mro() has not set base's MRO yet: its __base__ is asked too"] [1873 2 "// nothing more when a reentrant assignment replaced the bases"] [1892 1 "// newStaticBase is tp_new_wrapper's staticbase (REQUEST of PY6g for PY6-core: test_descr's test_bad_new): t, or"] [1893 1 "// the first base along __base__ whose __new__ is not a Python class's own (slot_tp_new)."] [1901 1 "// newOrigin is the built-in type whose __new__ t's tp_new is (inherited along __base__ from the first one"] [1902 1 "// that defines it), CPython's tp_new pointer compared."] [1916 1 "// newAliases: the built-in types whose own __new__ here is CPython's inherited one (defaultdict's is dict_new)"] [1919 1 "// isNewWrapper: v is a built-in type's __new__ (tp_new_wrapper); a class whose __new__ is one keeps t